WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.298 --> 00:00:02.886
Everyone wants to build the next billion-dollar startup.

2
00:00:03.613 --> 00:00:06.586
But what if the next useful product is something much smaller?

3
00:00:08.395 --> 00:00:10.318
Think about the person running a small shop.

4
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.199
They make sales all day,

5
00:00:12.329 --> 00:00:15.245
receive transfers, pay suppliers, cover expenses,

6
00:00:15.365 --> 00:00:17.198
and somehow, at the end of the month,

7
00:00:17.318 --> 00:00:18.940
they still don't know where the money went.

8
00:00:20.396 --> 00:00:21.749
And this isn't imaginary.

9
00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.742
Research involving seven hundred and eighteen Nigerian microbusinesses found that

10
00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:28.235
sixty-four percent kept no financial records.

11
00:00:28.924 --> 00:00:32.077
Only thirty-two percent separated business money from personal money.

12
00:00:33.196 --> 00:00:34.780
Now imagine something simpler.

13
00:00:35.473 --> 00:00:37.693
Not another complicated accounting platform.

14
00:00:38.343 --> 00:00:40.411
Just a tool that records what comes in,

15
00:00:40.531 --> 00:00:42.774
what goes out, and what is actually left.

16
00:00:43.695 --> 00:00:47.369
A sale comes in: twelve thousand five hundred naira, bank transfer.

17
00:00:48.049 --> 00:00:48.547
Saved.

18
00:00:49.287 --> 00:00:51.226
Transport takes one thousand eight hundred.

19
00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:52.466
Saved.

20
00:00:53.206 --> 00:00:55.090
A personal withdrawal is marked separately,

21
00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.690
so it never gets confused with a business expense.

22
00:00:58.364 --> 00:01:00.665
At closing time: sales, expenses,

23
00:01:00.785 --> 00:01:03.253
personal withdrawals, and what is actually left.

24
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.337
Just the numbers that matter.

25
00:01:06.598 --> 00:01:07.758
And that's the point.

26
00:01:08.548 --> 00:01:11.541
You don't always need to invent something nobody has ever seen.

27
00:01:12.226 --> 00:01:15.261
Sometimes, you just need to notice what people struggle with,

28
00:01:15.381 --> 00:01:18.470
remove the friction, and make their everyday lives a little easier.

29
00:01:19.496 --> 00:01:22.454
Maybe your first successful startup doesn't need a million users.

30
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.741
Just a thousand people who don't want to live without it.
